# Skode Audio: Browser WebAssembly Synthesis

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino, "~> 0.14"}
])
```

## Overview

[Skode](https://github.com/octetta/skode) is a micro-language and BEAM/JS client for the native [Pulp](https://github.com/octetta/pulp) audio synthesis engine.

This Livebook notebook demonstrates **zero-dependency browser audio**:
* **100% Client-Side Synthesis**: The native Pulp C DSP engine runs as WebAssembly directly inside your browser at 44.1 kHz via the Web Audio API.
* **Zero Server Audio Drivers**: Your Livebook host (local workstation, remote server, Docker container, or Fly.io instance) requires **no** ALSA, PulseAudio, PipeWire, Jack, or C compilation toolchain.
* **Reactive Elixir Control**: Elixir cells send Skode commands down to the browser audio engine in real time using `Kino.JS.Live`.

> **Note**: When Skode is released on Hex.pm, you will also be able to add `{:skode, "~> 0.3"}` to `Mix.install/1` to use Skode's Gleam/Elixir builder API.

---

## 1. Define the Livebook Audio Component

The `SkodeAudio` module uses `Kino.JS.Live` to load the official Pulp WebAssembly binary from `https://octetta.github.io/skode/wasm/skred_api.js` and bridge Elixir events to the engine.

```elixir
defmodule SkodeAudio do
  use Kino.JS
  use Kino.JS.Live

  @doc """
  Create a new Skode WebAssembly audio widget.
  """
  def new() do
    Kino.JS.Live.new(__MODULE__, nil)
  end

  @doc """
  Send a Skode command string to the WebAssembly engine.
  """
  def play(kino, command) when is_binary(command) do
    Kino.JS.Live.cast(kino, {:play, command})
  end

  @doc """
  Stop all active voices immediately (panic).
  """
  def stop(kino) do
    Kino.JS.Live.cast(kino, :stop)
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Kino.JS.Live Server Callbacks
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @impl true
  def init(_payload, ctx) do
    {:ok, assign(ctx, status: :ready)}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_connect(ctx) do
    {:ok, %{}, ctx}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_cast({:play, command}, ctx) do
    broadcast_event(ctx, "play", %{command: command})
    {:noreply, ctx}
  end

  @impl true
  def handle_cast(:stop, ctx) do
    broadcast_event(ctx, "stop", %{})
    {:noreply, ctx}
  end

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Browser-Side JavaScript Asset
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  asset "main.js" do
    """
    export function init(ctx, data) {
      ctx.root.innerHTML = `
        <div style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; background: #161b22; color: #c9d1d9; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px; margin-bottom: 8px;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 10px;">
            <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
              <span style="font-weight: 600; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px;">Skode / Pulp WebAssembly Engine</span>
              <span id="badge" style="font-size: 11px; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 10px; background: #21262d; border: 1px solid #30363d; color: #8b949e;">Loading WASM...</span>
            </div>
            <div style="display: flex; gap: 8px;">
              <button id="btn-start" style="background: #238636; color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(240,246,252,0.1); border-radius: 6px; padding: 5px 12px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer;">
                Start Audio Engine
              </button>
              <button id="btn-panic" style="background: #da3633; color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(240,246,252,0.1); border-radius: 6px; padding: 5px 12px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer;">
                Panic / Stop
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div id="log" style="font-family: monospace; font-size: 12px; background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 12px; height: 95px; overflow-y: auto; color: #7ee787;">
            [pulp] Initializing...
          </div>
        </div>
      `;

      const logEl = ctx.root.querySelector("#log");
      const badgeEl = ctx.root.querySelector("#badge");
      const btnStart = ctx.root.querySelector("#btn-start");
      const btnPanic = ctx.root.querySelector("#btn-panic");

      function log(msg) {
        if (!logEl) return;
        const line = document.createElement("div");
        line.textContent = msg;
        logEl.appendChild(line);
        logEl.scrollTop = logEl.scrollHeight;
      }

      function setBadge(text, color, bg) {
        if (!badgeEl) return;
        badgeEl.textContent = text;
        badgeEl.style.color = color;
        badgeEl.style.background = bg;
      }

      window.Module = window.Module || {};
      if (!window.Module.locateFile) {
        window.Module.locateFile = function(path) {
          return "https://octetta.github.io/skode/wasm/" + path;
        };
      }

      function loadScript(url) {
        return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
          if (window.Module && (window.Module._skred_start || window.Module.ccall)) {
            return resolve();
          }
          const existing = document.querySelector("script[data-skode-wasm]");
          if (existing) {
            if (window.Module && window.Module._skred_start) return resolve();
            existing.addEventListener("load", () => resolve());
            existing.addEventListener("error", (e) => reject(e));
            return;
          }
          const s = document.createElement("script");
          s.dataset.skodeWasm = "true";
          s.src = url;
          s.async = true;
          s.onload = () => resolve();
          s.onerror = (e) => reject(e);
          document.head.appendChild(s);
        });
      }

      let engineStarted = false;

      function startAudio() {
        try {
          if (window.Module && typeof window.Module._skred_start === "function") {
            if (!engineStarted) {
              window.Module._skred_start(128, 16, 0);
              engineStarted = true;
            }
            if (typeof window.Module._skred_logger === "function") {
              window.Module._skred_logger(1);
            }
            setBadge("Engine Active", "#56d364", "#23863622");
            log("[pulp] WebAudio active (128 frames, 16 voices, 44.1 kHz).");
          } else {
            log("[pulp] WebAssembly module not ready yet.");
          }
        } catch (err) {
          log("[pulp] Start error: " + err);
        }
      }

      function executeCommand(cmd) {
        if (!window.Module || typeof window.Module.ccall !== "function") {
          log("[pulp] Cannot send: WASM module not loaded.");
          return;
        }
        if (!engineStarted && typeof window.Module._skred_start === "function") {
          startAudio();
        }
        const lines = cmd.split("\\n");
        for (const line of lines) {
          const trimmed = line.trim();
          if (trimmed) {
            log("> " + trimmed);
            window.Module.ccall("skred_command", "number", ["string"], [trimmed]);
            try {
              const out = window.Module.ccall("skred_log", "string", [], []);
              if (out && out.trim()) {
                log(out.trim());
              }
            } catch (_) {}
          }
        }
      }

      btnStart.addEventListener("click", () => startAudio());
      btnPanic.addEventListener("click", () => {
        executeCommand("K");
        log("[pulp] All voices killed.");
      });

      loadScript("https://octetta.github.io/skode/wasm/skred_api.js")
        .then(() => {
          setBadge("Ready to Start", "#58a6ff", "#1f6feb22");
          log("[pulp] WASM binary loaded from CDN. Click 'Start Audio Engine'.");
        })
        .catch((err) => {
          setBadge("Load Error", "#f85149", "#da363322");
          log("[pulp] Failed to load WASM: " + err);
        });

      ctx.handleEvent("play", ({ command }) => executeCommand(command));
      ctx.handleEvent("stop", () => executeCommand("K"));
    }
    """
  end
end
```

---

## 2. Boot the Audio Engine

Evaluate the cell below to render the Skode Audio widget.

> **Important**: Click **Start Audio Engine** on the widget before triggering notes. Web browsers require a user gesture on the page to un-mute the Web Audio subsystem.

```elixir
audio = SkodeAudio.new()
```

---

## 3. Play Notes and Polyphonic Chords

Skode commands configure voices (`v0`..`v15`), waveforms (`w`), frequencies (`f`), amplitudes (`a` in dB), and trigger envelopes (`T`).

Let's play an **A Major Triad** across 3 voices:
* Voice 0: A3 (220.00 Hz)
* Voice 1: C#4 (277.18 Hz)
* Voice 2: E4 (329.63 Hz)

```elixir
SkodeAudio.play(audio, """
v0 w1 f220.00 a-6 T
v1 w1 f277.18 a-6 T
v2 w1 f329.63 a-6 T
""")
```

---

## 4. Waveforms & Resonant Filters

Pulp offers classic and hybrid synthesizer waveforms:
* `w1` - Sawtooth
* `w2` - Square / Pulse (with `w10`..`w90` pulse widths)
* `c<hz>` - Low-pass filter cutoff frequency
* `q<val>` - Filter resonance / Q factor

Let's trigger a deep resonant bass pulse:

```elixir
SkodeAudio.play(audio, "v0 w20 f110.00 a-3 c600 q5 T")
```

---

## 5. Algorithmic Sequencer in Elixir

Because Elixir manages concurrency and timing, we can sequence patterns using simple Elixir loops or `Task`:

```elixir
arpeggio = [
  220.00, # A3
  277.18, # C#4
  329.63, # E4
  440.00, # A4
  554.37, # C#5
  659.25, # E5
  880.00  # A5
]

for _cycle <- 1..2, freq <- arpeggio do
  SkodeAudio.play(audio, "v0 w1 f#{freq} a-8 T")
  Process.sleep(125)
end
```

---

## 6. Ksynth SID Chiptune Sounds (Commodore 64)

Pulp 0.85.0 includes the **Ksynth** SID emulation engine (`w300`..`w302`):
* `w300` - SID 6581 Triangle
* `w301` - SID 6581 Sawtooth
* `w302` - SID 6581 Pulse

Let's trigger an 8-bit chiptune lead:

```elixir
SkodeAudio.play(audio, """
v0 w300 f261.63 a-4 T
v1 w302 f523.25 a-8 T
""")
```

---

## 7. Stop / Silence All Voices

To instantly silence all active voices:

```elixir
SkodeAudio.stop(audio)
```
